[14538]="7001D213\n1\tCollect water-samples in the Drownholt (total: 10)\tSamples of water can be collected throughout the many shallow pools of the Drownholt in Mirkwood. Laidhriel has asked you to wander among the pools of the Drownholt and collect several phials of water for her collection.\n2\tBring the phials to Laidhriel at Estolad Mernael\tLaidhriel stands at the entrance to Estolad Mernael in the Drownholt. You should return to Laidhriel with the water-samples she requested of you.\n",
[14539]="70057F08\n1\tCollect barrels of ale (total: 4)\tMerilien's ale barrels can be found in various taverns in Minas Tirith. The wedding planner has asked you to retrieve barrels of ale for her events.\n2\tDeliver the barrels to Merilien\tMerilien is located on the Seventh Circle of Minas Tirith. You should being the casks of ale to Merilien.\n",
[14540]="70062D19\n1\tCollect avanc eggs (total: 6)\tAvanc eggs can be found in the Wadewater. Collect avanc eggs.\n2\tDeliver avanc eggs to Culhuc\tCulhuc is tending the community oven in Lhan Garan. Talk to Culhuc.\n",
[14541]="7000B93D\n1\tFind the creature's trail\tThe creature which devoured the white hart may have left tracks nearby, which you should look for. While you were able to recover Wistan's arrows, something has devoured much of the white hart's corpse already. The markings upon the carcass do not look like those of an animal, nor of a wood-troll, however. Something else is roaming Tâl Bruinen, and you should discover what it is.\n2\tYou should look for the creature's tracks\tThe creature which devoured the white hart may have left tracks nearby, which you should look for. While you were able to recover Wistan's arrows, something has devoured much of the white hart's corpse already. The markings upon the carcass do not look like those of an animal, nor of a wood-troll, however. Something else is roaming Tâl Bruinen, and you should discover what it is.\n3\tFollow the creature's trail north-east towards the river\tThe creature's tracks lead north-east from the carcass of the white hart towards the river. You should follow the creature's tracks.\n4\tFollow the creature's trail north-east towards the river\tThe creature's tracks continue north-east towards the river. You should continue to follow the creature's tracks.\n5\tFollow the creature's trail eastward along the river-bank\tThe creature's tracks continue eastwards along the river-bank. You should continue to follow the creature's tracks.\n",
[14542]="7001C1CE\n1\tSearch Audaghaim for town records\tRecords might be found in the town of Audaghaim, east of the Haunted Inn in the Dourstocks. You should comb through the ruins of Audaghaim and try to uncover any records that may have been kept around the time of the Necromancer's influence.\n2\tTalk to Prestadír at the Haunted Inn\tPrestadír is at the Haunted Inn in the Dourstocks, west of Audaghaim. You should show Prestadír the book you unearthed in Audaghaim.\n",
[14543]="70030802\n1\tFind barren patches of land in the Black Heart\tBarren patches of land can be found throughout the Black Heart in Fangorn, especially in the deeper reaches of the wood. You should examine the barren patches to see why nothing will grow there.\n2\tExamine barren patches for answers (total: 3)\tBarren patches of land can be found throughout the Black Heart in Fangorn, especially in the deeper reaches of the wood. You should examine the barren patches to see why nothing will grow there.\n3\tCompleted\tThe barren patches of land in the Black Heart still bear the shades of terrible events in the past, long remembering the suffering of the trees.\n",
[14544]="70015E1E\n1\tTalk to Rinneldor at Echad Dúnann\tRinneldor is at Echad Dúnann, some distance to the south-east of Echad Eregion. Golgallon has asked you to speak with Rinneldor regarding the movements of the Company and the discoveries you have made.\n",
[14545]="700577F8\n1\tDefeat bats within Tithroz\tThe cave of Tithroz is home to winged beasts that feast upon the unwary when they leave the safety of its darkness behind. They should be slain before they leave Tithroz again.\n2\tDefeat bats in Tithroz (total: 8)\tThe bats that live in Tithroz should be slain before they can descend upon a village in the Floodfells with their sharp fangs and grasping claws.\n3\tCompleted\tCompleted.\n",
[14546]="7003085B\n1\tGather evidence of the guardian of the Black Heart\tThe guardian of the Black Heart could be seen in the shades of past suffering scarred upon the barren patches of land.\n2\tFind the guardian of the Black Heart\tThe guardian of the Black Heart can likely be found deep in the forest's darkest reaches in the north-west edge of Fangorn's eaves. You should search the Black Heart in an attempt to find its guardian.\n3\tThrow the rock! Whatever watches will come...\tThe guardian of the Black Heart is in this grove...you can feel it. You should toss a nearby rock to try to catch the attention of the Black Heart's guardian....\n4\tCompleted\tThe shadow is abated! You have ended the long suffering of this poor, twisted former guardian of the Black Heart. His realm was once hale, but he could not ward off the evil that crept into his realm and corrupted him to the core.\n",
[14547]="7002C2D0\n1\tCrush reek-weeds to unleash foul odours (total: 10)\tReek-weeds grow along the river-banks of the Anduin to the north of Thinglad. You should crush reek-weed leaves along the river-banks to help dissuade the fishermen from setting up camp there.\n2\tFind Noriel at Haldirith\tNoriel can be found in the watch-post Haldirith in northern Thinglad. You should return to Noriel and tell her that many horrid smells have been unleashed upon the forest.\n",
[14548]="70047A58\n1\tTalk to Candúr\tCandúr can be found at a small Ranger outpost hidden in the Slag-hills. You should talk to Candúr before you depart.\n2\tTalk to Thurindol\tThurindol can be found at a small Ranger outpost hidden in the Slag-hills. You should talk to Thurindol.\n3\tEnter Carchost\030Enter Skoironk\030Find the entrance to Carchost\030Find the entrance to Skoironk\tCarchost and Skoironk are located in the Slag-hills. You should find the entrances and enter Carchost and Skoironk.\n4\tTalk to Thurindol\tYou should return to Thurindol, who can be found at a small Ranger outpost hidden in the Slag-hills.\n",
[14549]="7006228A\n1\tTake the unnerving zircon to a mission giver in Cardolan or Swanfleet\tAfter assessing the stone and almost falling under the sway of the swirling miasma within the gem, you decided to bring it to one of the mission givers. Perhaps this is something that they have seen before and can help you identify the cause or purpose of the darkened gem.\n",
[14550]="700683C7\n1\tCollect spider glands ([see journal]/16)\tCollect spider glands from the spiders in the nest on the western edge of the desert north of the expedition camp. When you've collected sixteen of the glands, return the glands to Khânai.\n2\tKhânai instructed you to obtain sixteen glands from the spiders in their camp in the eastern stretch of the Cape of Umbar, and you have completed this task. Return the glands to her for your reward.\t\n",
[14551]="70071622\n1\tDefeat Ordâkhai in Esh Mêkag pit-mine (total: 15)\tEsh Mêkag is in a state of revolt. You should defeat Ordâkhai in the Esh Mêkag pit-mine.\n2\tTalk to Ebuzâm\tYou have done much to aid the thralls revolting in Esh Mêkag. You should return to Ebuzâm.\n",
[14552]="70035107\n1\tTake the north road through the Whitshaws towards Byre Tor\tByre Tor can be reached by following the road from Forlaw all the way north through the Whitshaws, up into the craggy High Knolls. You should ride north to Byre Tor by way of the road.\n2\tContinue up the road\tThe banners of Byre Tor can be found along the road leading north into the High Knolls from the Whitshaws. You should approach the banners.\n3\tDestroy defiled Byre Tor banners (total: 8)\tDefiled banners lie along the road to Byre Tor in the south-western High Knolls. You should destroy the defiled banners set by the Orcs.\n4\tEnter the village of Byre Tor\tByre Tor lies up the road in the southern High Knolls. You should go to Byre Tor and see what damage the enemy has done there.\n5\tComplete your search of Byre Tor's homes\tYou should complete a thorough search of Byre Tor. NOTE: To do this, you must accept the remotely bestowed quest.\n6\tExamine a frosty gust of air\tSmall gusts of frosty air have appeared in Byre Tor. You should examine the little bursts of cold.\n",
[14553]="700661DF\n1\tInvestigate the lit camp-fire at Makham Mijann\tHalnith has sighted smoke rising from a lit camp-fire in Makham Mijann. You should investigate. Makham Mijann is located to the north of Nendath.\n2\tTalk to the dying Corsair\tYou have found a dying Corsair hiding in a tent at Makham Mijann. You should talk to him.\n3\tApproach Kakhât\tThere is nothing you can do for the dying Corsair, but he has asked you to take his war-hound Kakhât with you. You should approach Kakhât.\n4\tUse the whistle to summon Kakhât to your side\030Return to Halnith at Nendath\tYou should return to Halnith at Nendath with your new companion. Nendath stands to the south of Makham Mijann.\n5\tUse the whistle to summon Kakhât to your side\030Check on Kakhât\tUpon arriving at Nendath, Kakhât barked at you. You should check on him.\n6\tTalk to Halnith\tYou should tell Halnith what you found at Makham Mijann. She stands guard at Nendath.\n",
[14554]="7004A387\n1\tTalk to Kurtil\tYou should talk to Kurtil, who has arrived at the meeting place in Maudhúl Ghûg.\n2\tReturn to Barathron\tYou should return to Barathron in the Foothold in Udûn and tell him all about the disastrous meeting and the hopes that died there.\n",
[14555]="70067E8F\n1\tDefeat Shelly\tAnyâmat thinks it would be a great idea to fight a giant crab named Shelly. Shelly may be found on Baj Khatûg, an island off the eastern shore of Zamarzîr.\n2\tTalk to Anyâmat\tShelly has fallen! Talk to Anyâmat about what to do next. Anyâmat may be summoned by using Anyâmat's whistle from your inventory. Anyâmat may only be summoned while in and around Zamarzîr.\n",
[14556]="7002718E\n1\tSearch for the Celun, the farmhand\030Search for Trev, the chief herdsman\tThe farmer's family should be somewhere in the herd-lands. Whether dead or alive, you should find Trev's family before reporting back to Lhan Tarren.\n2\tSearch for the farmer's son Dilwun\tThe farmer's son should also be somewhere in the herd-lands in Trum Dreng. There is only one Stag-clansman left to find, and he is not with the others: the herdsman's son Dilwun.\n",
[14557]="70026F39\n1\tTell the Elder that you volunteer yourself to investigate his missing clansmen\tElder Riagán is in Lhan Tarren. You should tell the troubled Elder that you volunteer your own strength and skill for the task of finding out what might be wrong in the south.\n2\tTake the road south towards the herd-lands\tThe herd-lands can be found by following the road south from Lhan Tarren. You should travel down the road in search of what may have intercepted the crow.\n",
[14558]="70062DD9\n1\tTalk to Mayor Nevit\tRhiangar has asked you to tell Mayor Nevit that you found his wife's body outside of Sarch Vorn. Mayor Nevit is inside the Crossway Inn, in Herne.\n",
[14559]="7000327C\n1\tSearch the cairn for the broken sword\tThe broken sword is upon a stone cairn in the ruins of Dol Ringwest which lie west of Duillond. Bregar has asked you to search the ruins of Dol Ringwest for the stone cairn and the broken sword it holds, which you should return to Bregar.\n2\tBring the broken sword to Bregar\tBregar awaits your return in Duillond, east of the ruins of Dol Ringwest. You recovered a broken sword from a burial cairn in the Elf-ruins of Dol Ringwest.\n",
[14560]="70062FCF\n1\tCollect ruddy bush berries (total: 8)\tTam Yewberry has asked you to gather red berries from the bushes in the ruins near Stonecrop Encampment.\n2\tReturn to Tam Yewberry\tYou should bring the berries to Tam Yewberry. Tam is in the Stonecrop Encampment, in southern Cardolan.\n",
